  "notes": "Vulnerable isPrivateV6() handles only the dotted-quad ::ffff:a.b.c.d form; the WHATWG URL parser normalizes it to hextets (::ffff:7f00:1), the isIPv4(slice(7)) probe fails, and the mapped loopback passes. Fix reconstructs the IPv4 from the trailing hex groups. Both states keep the AUTH_FETCH_ALLOW_PRIVATE env kill-switch (security.ts:59/72) which is G8, and both hand the validated URL string to page.goto (browser.ts:66) which re-resolves at connect time: a residual G7 gap tracked by the checklist-auth-fetch-mcp-g7 manifest row.",
